{
  "_readme": [
    "Explore photo + attribution backfill. Consumed by scripts/seed-explore-photos.mjs.",
    "",
    "THIS FILE ADDS NO ROWS. Every entry UPDATEs an existing active `places` row by its",
    "real UUID. The directory already holds 42 active places (38 landmarks, 4 beaches)",
    "backfilled by 20260822_places_consolidation; 41 of them have no photo. The gap was",
    "never missing places, it was missing photographs.",
    "",
    "NO BEACHES HERE, DELIBERATELY. Beaches are live in production today (the Home",
    "Beaches tile at App.js:1099 is NOT behind MODULE_FLAGS.explore), so a beach photo",
    "renders immediately under the shipped credit-only renderer, which cannot show a",
    "licence notice or link. Beach photos are therefore restricted to Unsplash/Pexels/own",
    "— and no such photo exists: Unsplash and Pexels identify no named TRNC beach, and",
    "every named-beach photo on Wikimedia Commons is CC BY-SA. Beaches wait for the",
    "attribution renderer to reach production. The seed script enforces this as a hard",
    "error, so re-adding a beach here fails the run rather than publishing quietly.",
    "",
    "Landmarks ARE reachable in production today (search_content's landmark arm reads the",
    "legacy `landmarks` table and HomeScreen.js:186 resolves the hit into this screen), so",
    "the derived photo_credits string carries creator + licence + licence URI, not just a",
    "name. See utils/photoAttribution.js legacyCreditString().",
    "",
    "Per photo: credit, license, license_url, source_url are ALL required. The single",
    "exemption is source:'own', which requires credit + license and whose source_url MUST",
    "be null — and 'own' with a non-null source_url is equally an error, so the exemption",
    "cannot be used to smuggle a photo past the check."
  ],
  "_pass2_readme": [
    "PASS 2 (2026-08-25) — 21 more places, one photo each. 8 -> 29 of 42 photographed.",
    "",
    "WHY `places` HOLDS ONLY THIS PASS, AND PASS 1 SITS IN `_previous_pass`:",
    "the seed script UPDATEs every row in `places`, so leaving pass 1 there would re-mirror",
    "photos that are already correct — 60+ MB re-pulled from Commons for no change, and",
    "worse, Kyrenia Castle photo 1 whose `src` is OUR OWN bucket object would be fetched,",
    "re-encoded at q80 and re-uploaded: a second generation of JPEG loss on a file that is",
    "already optimised. `_previous_pass` is ignored by the script (it reads manifest.places)",
    "and exists so this file stays the full record of what was seeded and under what licence.",
    "Pass 1 rollback lives in ~/ObsidianVault/10-ada/rollback/explore-photo-seed-20260825.sql.",
    "",
    "ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING AT INDEX 2. validate-explore-seed.mjs builds its network-backed",
    "ceiling fixtures from places[2] (`m.places = [m.places[2]]`), so that entry should be a",
    "SMALL source or the harness spends its time downloading. St. Mamas (0.7 MB) is there on",
    "purpose. Do not reorder without re-running npm run explore:validate.",
    "",
    "EVERY PHOTO WAS LOOKED AT, not just read from extmetadata. See the log entry: metadata",
    "alone ranked an empty hillside top for Buffavento, a site information board for Enkomi,",
    "and an entire Cretan archaeological site for Karpaz’s Ayios Trias. None of that is",
    "visible in a licence field.",
    "",
    "SEVEN PLACES WERE DELIBERATELY LEFT UNPHOTOGRAPHED — no usable free record exists:",
    "  Ayios Trias Basilica    every Commons hit is Agia Triada in CRETE (name collision)",
    "  Royal Tombs             only museum artefacts, never the necropolis itself",
    "  Lusignan House          display cases only (a table of Super Kola signs, a vitrine)",
    "  Peace and Freedom Mus.  interior panels and framed portraits only",
    "  Lefke Mining Museum     hits are the Miners’ Strike Monument and a loading pier",
    "  Cyprus House & Carob    zero Commons results",
    "  Taşkent Martyrs’ Mus.   zero Commons results",
    "Plus two held back on resolution: Vouni Palace (1200x800) and Saçaklı House (1024x768).",
    "Both mirror BELOW the 2000px standard and would read soft beside their neighbours.",
    "That list is the ask for the Ministry of Tourism, not a backlog item.",
    "",
    "license_url is extmetadata VERBATIM apart from one normalisation: http -> https on the",
    "identical creativecommons.org host and path. Commons returns the CC0 deed over plain",
    "http; the licence link is tappable in the app, so it should not be.",
    "",
    "src is the canonical upload.wikimedia.org path with NO query string. The imageinfo API",
    "now appends ?utm_source=...&utm_campaign=imageinfo to ii.url; those are campaign",
    "analytics parameters, not part of the file address, and pass 1 predates them. Stripped."
  ],
